      "sequence_position": 8,
      "problem": "Let $c=⟨2,-1,6⟩$ and $d=⟨4,-2,10⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $c$ onto $d.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{d\\cdot d}d \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{{d}_{x}^{2}+{d}_{y}^{2}+{d}_{z}^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+6\\cdot 10}{{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{10}^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{70}{120}⟨4,-2,10⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{12}⟨4,-2,10⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\,\\frac{7}{3},-\\frac{7}{6},\\frac{35}{6}\\,⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
